<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Treasury's latest economic outlook table.</title>
<headline>NZ Treasury's latest economic outlook table.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the budget economic outlook table released by the New Zealand Treasury on Thursday.</p>
<p>The forecasts are for March years, annual average percentage change, apart from: Unemployment rate (HLFS unemployment as a percentage of labour force, s/adj, Mar qtr), 90-day bank bills (average for March qtr), core inflation (annual pct change, Mar qtr), current account NZ$billion. GDP is production based.</p>
<p>Brackets contain projections published in the December Fiscal and Economic Update.  </p>
<p>				  1997/98     1998/99     1999/00</p>
<p>Private consumption	 1.9 (4.7)   4.5 (3.5)   3.5 (3.5)</p>
<p>Private investment	  2.9 (8.7)  10.2 (5.6)   7.4 (6.6)</p>
<p>Exports			 2.8 (4.0)   5.8 (5.2)   5.3 (5.6)</p>
<p>Imports			 5.2 (5.2)   8.9 (6.7)   4.9 (4.0)</p>
<p>GDP			     2.4 (3.6)   4.2 (3.1)   3.5 (3.5)</p>
<p>Unemployment rate (%)     6.8 (6.1)   6.2 (6.0)   5.7 (5.7)</p>
<p>90-day bill rate (%)	7.6 (8.0)   8.6 (7.3)   7.4 (6.3)</p>
<p>Core inflation (%)	  1.0 (1.2)   1.3 (1.5)   1.6 (1.2)</p>
<p>Current account balance -4.9 (-4.3) -5.7 (-4.9) -5.0 (-4.0)</p>
<p>Current a/c pct/GDP     -5.0 (-4.3) -5.5 (-4.6) -4.6 (-3.6)</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
